## What it actually does

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    IN["prompt<br/>(any mix of types)"] --> FE
    subgraph FE["front-end"]
      direction TB
      O["structural oracles<br/>ast.parse · json.loads"]
      S["Viterbi region segmentation"]
      P["8 typed pipelines"]
      O --> S --> P
    end
    FE --> IR["<b>Context IR</b><br/>units × fidelity ladders<br/>obligations · protection lattice · edges"]
    IR --> MID
    subgraph MID["middle-end"]
      direction TB
      D["semantic dedup + delta"]
      A["phantom attention (PPR)"]
      C["CASCADE — submodular MCKP"]
      K["dependency closure"]
      D --> A --> C --> K
    end
    MID --> BE
    subgraph BE["back-end"]
      direction TB
      R["render → context bytecode"]
      V["verify: provenance · obligations<br/>syntax · inflation · frozen"]
      F["confidence + adaptive loop"]
      R --> V --> F
    end
    BE --> OUT["compressed context<br/>+ audit report<br/>+ recovery handles"]
    V -.repair.-> R
    F -.raise budget.-> C
```

**The key structural idea.** Every unit has a *fidelity ladder*, so selection is
a multiple-choice knapsack rather than keep-or-drop:

```
drop  <  signature  <  signature + doc  <  full body
 0 tok    11 tok        18 tok             184 tok
```

At a tight budget, LLMLingua must choose between the whole function and nothing.
ULRC³ buys the 11-token contract. That is the difference between 100% and 37.5%
identifier retention on mixed content.

### Example: a Python module at 60% compression

```python
import logging
from dataclasses import dataclass
logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)
MAX_RETRIES = 3
TIMEOUT_MS = 250
@dataclass
class Receipt:
    ...
class PaymentGateway:
    def __init__(self, api_key: str, base_url: str = "https://api.acme.io/v2") -> None: ...
    def charge(self, customer_id: str, amount_cents: int, currency: str = "USD") -> Receipt: ...
    def refund(self, receipt_id: str, amount_cents: int) -> Receipt: ...
def _make_id(customer_id: str, amount_cents: int) -> str:
    seed = f"{customer_id}:{amount_cents}"
    return f"rcpt_{abs(hash(seed)) % 10**12:012d}"
def duplicate_make_id(user_id: str, cents: int) -> str: ...   # == _make_id
```

Every signature **byte-identical**. Every needed import kept. Duplicate
implementation detected by Merkle AST hash. Module still parses. Verified.

---

## Content types

| type | strategy |
|---|---|
| **code** | AST → symbol table → def-use graph → program slice; bodies elide to verbatim signatures; imports pruned *by closure*; duplicates by Merkle hash; output re-parsed |
| **conversation** | typed memory records → belief revision DAG; corrections retract their antecedent *and its answer*; verbatim recency window |
| **logs** | Drain-style template mining; `template ×N @window {slots}`; ERROR/FATAL and singletons floored above drop |
| **JSON/YAML** | schema induction with optional/enum/format detection + k samples + stats; **every key preserved** |
| **RAG** | query never compressed; water-filled per-chunk budgets; cross-chunk delta encoding; contrastive relevance |
| **tables/SQL** | header locked; deterministic column profile; DDL locked; identifiers as obligations |
| **legal** | clause-granular, order-preserving, cross-reference edges, defined terms anchored |
| **API docs** | endpoints, parameter rows, status codes locked |
| **mixed** | all of the above, per region, in one document |

---

## Results (matched budgets, 156 instances)

| system | ratio | answerability | contradictions | numbers | identifiers | hallucinated |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **ULRC³ balanced** | **75.3%** | **100.0%** | **0.0%** | **87.2%** | **99.4%** | **0** |
| selective_context | 74.6% | 85.8% | 11.1% | 70.6% | 79.9% | 0 |
| tfidf + MMR | 74.9% | 83.0% | 11.1% | 77.0% | 86.7% | 0 |
| llmlingua-style | 74.3% | 74.9% | 11.1% | 84.3% | 79.6% | 0 |
| truncate (head) | 74.1% | 33.2% | 11.1% | 41.9% | 77.2% | 0 |

Every one of the nine suites scores **100% answerability** at the balanced
operating point.

Selected suites where the architecture shows:

- **Logs** — ULRC³ 100% answerability at 98.7% compression; **every baseline 0%**.
- **Memory** — ULRC³ 0% contradiction; every importance-based baseline **100%**
  (they keep the retracted price *and* the current one).
- **Needle** — 100% retention at **97.1%** compression (34×), depth-independent.
- **Mixed** — 100% identifiers vs 37.5% for token-level deletion.

Performance: 41–44k tok/s **flat** from 1.4k to 128k tokens; 56 MB peak RSS at
64k; 2.90× process-pool speedup; 1 067× on cached documents.

### Ablation — including the result that went against us

`make ablation` disables each mechanism and re-runs everything:

| removing | Δ compression | Δ answerability |
|---|---|---|
| audit + repair loop | +1.6 | **−36.9** |
| fidelity ladder | **−4.6** | ±0.0 |
| semantic dedup | −1.4 | −0.3 |
| submodular coverage | −0.6 | ±0.0 |
| **Phantom Attention** | **−0.1** | **±0.0** |

Phantom Attention — one of the headline algorithms — earns ~0.1 points and no
measurable quality, and still earns nothing when the objective that could have
masked it is also removed. We report it, and the roadmap recommends deleting the
module if the extrinsic harness agrees.

The finding underneath it is the interesting one: on fact-bearing context,
**constraint satisfaction dominates importance ranking** — the half of the
problem the entire field optimises is the half that matters least here.

---

## Guarantees (all tested, all measured)

| | promise | measured |
|---|---|---|
| **Integrity** | Nothing retained is partially destroyed — no half-deleted number, truncated URL, or stripped negation | **100%** |
| **Critical recall** | Constraints, security policies, negations survive wherever they occur | **100%** |
| **Frozen** | System prompt, tools, instruction, query byte-identical, unreorderable | **100%** |
| **Zero hallucination** | Output words ⊆ input words ∪ markers | **0 violations** |
| **No inflation** | `tokens_out < tokens_in`, always | enforced |
| **Code parses** | Emitted Python re-parsed with `ast.parse` | enforced |
| **JSON keys** | Every key at every ratio | **100%** |
| **Determinism** | Same input + config ⇒ byte-identical output | enforced |

And what we **do not** promise — every numeral inside aggregate content, budget
over protection, semantic paraphrase, perfect belief revision — is listed with
equal prominence in [GUARANTEES.md](docs/GUARANTEES.md).

```bash
python -m pytest tests/ -q      # 235 tests
ulrc3 verify your_document.md   # exit 1 on any violation
```

